# ACT ONE

= Mara returns to the lighthouse she swore she'd never see again.

FADE IN:

EXT. CLIFFSIDE ROAD - DUSK #1#

Wind whips the grass flat. A battered hatchback crawls up the road.
Its headlights catch the LIGHTHOUSE, dark against a bruised sky.

[[Drone shot? Check budget.]]

MARA (V.O.)
My father kept the light burning for forty years.
He said the sea never forgives a dark night.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - KITCHEN - NIGHT #2#

Dust. Mara sets a box on the table. *Very* carefully.

MARA
(to herself)
Okay. Okay.
Just one night.

/* Cut for length:
Mara finds the old logbook under the sink.
She reads the last entry aloud.
*/

A KNOCK at the door. Mara freezes. [[sound design: three slow knocks]]

JONAS (O.S.)
Mara? It's Jonas. From the harbor.

MARA ^
Go away, Jonas.

.FLASHBACK - THE LAMP ROOM

!SILENCE.

~The keeper's song, the keeper's song

> THE END <

